  "synopsis": "The Meridian Star went dark in the South Atlantic for eleven days and came back wrong: logbook immaculate, crew answering a half-second too late, one hold welded shut — from the inside. Insurer's investigator Sarah Venn, ex-navy and allergic to mysteries, has seventy-two hours to clear her for re-departure. Instead she finds ballast records that make the ship heavier than physics allows, and a manifest listing forty containers loaded across three different centuries, the oldest sealed in 1911. The owners — a consortium of the world's great shipping houses — do not want her searched. They want her sunk on schedule, as she has apparently been sunk before. Because the Star is not carrying contraband. She is a filing cabinet: a century of evidence no court, port or government on earth wants to land.",
