  "tagline": "Vacancy. No questions. One mistake.",
  "synopsis": "Exit 47 is an interchange Florida forgot it built: one motel, one diner, one swamp. Ray Delgado, an ex-accountant who fled a fraud indictment and a marriage in the same week, works the Starlite's night desk under a simple system — cash, no questions, forget every face. It works until the faces repeat wrong: guests leave in other people's cars, a preacher checks in under three names in a month, and the woman in Room 6 leaves behind a suitcase containing thirty years of motel registration cards — including Ray's own, from the night he arrived. A state investigator mapping nine missing persons, a syndicate fixer who treats the motel as a family business, and Ray's buried past converge on the desk. He has one night to decide whether a man who built a life out of not noticing can afford to finally pay attention.",
