  "tagline": "One last job. Nap permitting.",
  "synopsis": "The Marlowe Street crew were never caught, because their one important job was never reported. In 1984 they lifted a corrupt developer's strongbox, and safecracker Dot Kowalczyk hid its irreplaceable contents — love letters that clear her late husband's name — inside the First Mercantile vault wall during the getaway. Now the Mercantile is demolished in sixty days, and Dot, eighty-one, reassembles the crew: getaway driver Sal, whose license and eyesight are both negotiable; forger Miriam, now the parish calligrapher, who denies nothing; and Eddie, the inside man, who took a janitor's job at the bank in 1985 as cover and simply never left. The plan must work around medications, hearing aids, and a security system installed by Dot's grandson. What they are stealing is worthless to everyone else on Earth — exactly why four old thieves will risk their only remaining asset, their legend, to steal it back.",
