  "logline": "A luxury brand trip strands six influencers and one very tired boat mechanic on an uninhabited island when the yacht's electronics die. Their combined survival skills are: unboxing, bronzing, and a dance that once ended a feud with a K-pop star. The tide, unfortunately, does not take brand deals.",
  "tagline": "Twelve million followers. Zero bars.",
  "synopsis": "The content yacht Marisol was meant to spend three days manufacturing spontaneity around a seltzer launch. Instead, a solar storm cooks her electronics twenty miles from the nearest shore, marooning six of the most-followed people on the Pacific with no signal, a cargo of ring lights and sponsored rations, and one crew member: mechanic Tomas Ibarra, below deck, asleep and contractually invisible. Fitness guru Brock attempts leadership by live-streaming to the ocean. Wellness heiress Sage declares a detox retreat and tries to charge for it. Only Tomas can fix the beacon, and Tomas — who has watched these people film his hands without asking for three seasons — names a price that is not money: each of them must do one genuinely useful thing, on camera, that no one will ever see. A dark comedy about the difference between an audience and a witness.",
