  "logline": "The sun is going out the way a hearth does — unevenly, with long cold mornings. Apprentice firekeeper Ash, seventeen and unlicensed, must carry the world's last living flame in a clay lantern across three kingdoms at war, because every army on the continent agrees on one thing: whoever holds the fire decides what survives the dark.",
