  "synopsis": "In 2041, the wealthy legally purchase other people's memories as luxury experience. June Park, 34, catalogs lots for the Vesper Exchange and has never questioned where the stock comes from — until a routine lot plays back her own seventh birthday, filmed from inside her mother's eyes. June was told her memories were wiped in a childhood accident. They were not. They were sold, in 41 separate lots, by a guardian she trusted. Teaming with a disgraced retrieval specialist who erases stolen memories for the desperate, June bids, steals and trades her way up the buyer chain toward the one lot nobody will list: the night her mother disappeared. Every memory she recovers changes what she believes — and the Exchange will burn its own archive before it lets her remember everything.",
