  "logline": "In the Republic, the Foresight Index predicts crimes before they happen and quietly moves polling places, patrols and futures accordingly — until an election auditor discovers the system has predicted her own crime, scheduled for next Tuesday.",
  "tagline": "Your future has already voted.",
  "synopsis": "Thirty years from now, the Republic governs by the Foresight Index, a model that predicts crime with celebrated accuracy: patrols surge where violence is predicted, and every election, 'high-risk' districts find their polling places consolidated for public safety. Election auditor Ingrid Halvorsen, 45, has certified it for a decade and believes in it as actuaries believe in tables. Auditing a disputed result, she finds a sealed annex in her own file: the Index predicts, with 91 percent confidence, that she will commit a violent felony next Tuesday, at an address she has never visited, alongside a man she will meet only because the prediction introduces them. As the state moves — lawfully, gently, irreversibly — to pre-manage her life, Ingrid joins the underground of the 'flagged' to ask the Republic's question in public: is a person what they do, or what they were predicted to do?",
